Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||11-16-2000||11:30 PM||||It does fairly well. Just pay attention to your wireing harness and brake lines.<BR>Make sure you have the A/C compressor and lines in a safe location.<BR>Again, KEEP YOUR EYES OPEN!||||reg||1
Z||000002||mshill||11-16-2000||11:37 PM||||Use the search function.  If it is not covered in the Haynes manual it is covered here somewhere.<P>I just finished dropping my second one in nine months.  The first time I started and tried to disconnect all the sensors and stuff.  I finally ended up just disconnecting the harness inside and dropping it with the cradle.  I have done both of mine solo with two floorjacks and a 4x4.  I also made a cradle dolly out of two furniture dollys and two 2x4s.<BR>||||reg||1
